---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Example from '../components/Example.astro';

const installHtml = `<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="lepidus.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <!-- your page -->
  <script src="lepidus.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>`;

const themeSwitch = `// the whole feature is one attribute — every token re-resolves
document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark'); // 'light' | 'dark' | 'hc'`;

const reactQuickstart = `import '@lepidus/tokens/build/css/tokens.css';
import { Button, Badge } from '@lepidus/react';

export function ReportToolbar() {
  return (
    <>
      <Button variant="primary">Run scan</Button>
      <Badge variant="success">14 servers healthy</Badge>
    </>
  );
}`;
---

<Page
  title="Get started"
  eyebrow="Start here"
  lede="Your first on-brand Lepide screen takes about five minutes: one stylesheet, copy-paste markup, three themes for free. Pick your path."
>
  <ul class="path-grid" aria-label="Choose your path">
    <li>
      <a class="path-card" href="#html">
        <span class="path-card__icon" style="background:#e9f0ff" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1c4599" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m8 7-5 5 5 5M16 7l5 5-5 5"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong>I write HTML/CSS/JS</strong>
          <small>The default path — start at step 1</small>
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="path-card" href="#react">
        <span class="path-card__icon" style="background:#e4f3ec" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#176639" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.2"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="10" ry="4.2"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="10" ry="4.2" transform="rotate(60 12 12)"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="10" ry="4.2" transform="rotate(120 12 12)"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong>My project is React</strong>
          <small>Typed components, same tokens</small>
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="path-card" href="/foundations/">
        <span class="path-card__icon" style="background:#fdf1e2" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#8a5b00" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 19a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 2.4-2.4h4.2A2.4 2.4 0 0 0 21 14.2V6a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-5.5"/><path d="M12 19a2.4 2.4 0 0 0-2.4-2.4H5.4A2.4 2.4 0 0 1 3 14.2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5.5"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong>I design</strong>
          <small>Foundations, themes, and the token language</small>
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="path-card" href="/ai/">
        <span class="path-card__icon" style="background:#f0ebfa" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#6d5bd0" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3v2M12 19v2M3 12h2M19 12h2M5.6 5.6l1.4 1.4M17 17l1.4 1.4M18.4 5.6 17 7M7 17l-1.4 1.4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong>I'm using an AI assistant</strong>
          <small>Point it at the AI surface and review the diff</small>
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="step" id="html"><span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>Get the files</h2>
  <p>
    Copy <code>lepidus.css</code> and <code>lepidus.js</code> from
    <code>packages/css/dist/</code> into your project and link them. That's the whole install —
    no npm, no bundler, nothing to configure. <code>lepidus.css</code> carries the design tokens
    and every component; <code>lepidus.js</code> (4&nbsp;KB) adds behavior to the interactive ones.
  </p>
  <Code code={installHtml} lang="html" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2 class="step"><span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>Ship your first component</h2>
  <p>
    Say you're building the toolbar for an audit report. Grab the markup from the
    <a href="/components/button/code/">Button</a> and <a href="/components/badge/code/">Badge</a>
    pages, paste, done — it renders like this, and it's live below (hover the buttons, tab
    through them):
  </p>
  <Example snippet="get-started/first-component" title="A report toolbar — your first paste" story="actions-button--primary" />
  <p>
    Every class follows one naming rule: block (<code>lp-button</code>), modifier
    (<code>lp-button--primary</code>), element (<code>lp-button__icon-left</code>). If a class
    isn't in the docs, it doesn't exist — the
    <a href="/components/">component pages</a> are the complete vocabulary.
  </p>

  <h2 class="step"><span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>Flip the theme</h2>
  <p>
    Press <strong>Dark</strong> in the example above. That's the entire feature: every color on
    the page is a CSS variable that re-resolves when <code>data-theme</code> changes on
    <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>. No second stylesheet, no theme classes, nothing to maintain.
  </p>
  <Code code={themeSwitch} lang="js" theme="github-dark" />
  <Callout variant="info" title="The one rule that makes this work">
    <p>Never hardcode a color, size, or radius — use the <a href="/tokens/">token variables</a>:
    <code>var(--component-*)</code> first, semantic <code>var(--color-*)</code> /
    <code>var(--space-*)</code> / <code>var(--radius-*)</code> otherwise. Hardcode one hex value
    and dark mode breaks exactly there.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 class="step"><span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>Add behavior</h2>
  <p>
    Interactive components work Bootstrap-style: write the documented markup, and
    <code>lepidus.js</code> wires it up — modals trap focus, tabs handle arrow keys, dropdowns
    close on Escape. Try it: this button raises a real toast, and "View incident" carries a
    tooltip.
  </p>
  <Example snippet="get-started/interactive" title="Behavior from lepidus.js — no code written" height={210} story="feedback-toast--info" />
  <p>
    The pattern is always the same: a <code>data-lp-*</code> attribute on the markup
    (<code>data-lp-tabs</code>, <code>data-lp-modal-open</code>, <code>data-lp-tooltip</code>)
    or a one-line JS call (<code>Lepidus.toast(&#123;…&#125;)</code>). Each component's Code tab
    shows exactly which.
  </p>

  <h2 class="step" id="react"><span class="step__num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>On React? Same system, typed</h2>
  <p>
    <code>@lepidus/react</code> renders pixel-identically to the plain-CSS classes — both are
    generated from the same source. Props are documented on every component's Specifications
    tab, extracted from the source with react-docgen, so they can't drift.
  </p>
  <Code code={reactQuickstart} lang="tsx" theme="github-dark" />
  <p>
    The <a href="/storybook/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Storybook ↗</a> is the interactive
    workshop behind everything on this site — every state of every component, switchable across
    all three themes and RTL.
  </p>

  <h2>The four rules</h2>
  <p class="home-section__sub">Everything else is convention; these four are enforced by CI.</p>
  <ul class="rule-grid">
    <li class="rule-card">
      <strong>Tokens, not hex values</strong>
      <p>Hardcoded colors fail the build. The payoff: dark and high-contrast themes work everywhere, forever, for free.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="rule-card">
      <strong>Keep the documented ARIA</strong>
      <p>The markup you copy already passes axe — <code>role="switch"</code> on toggles, <code>aria-invalid</code> on errors. Strip it and CI catches it.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="rule-card">
      <strong>Don't fight the shape</strong>
      <p>Buttons and inputs are pill-shaped by token. Overriding radii is the fastest way to make a screen feel un-Lepide.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="rule-card">
      <strong>AI-generated UI gets reviewed too</strong>
      <p>Point assistants at the <a href="/ai/">AI surface</a> so they generate real <code>lp-</code> classes — then hold the output to the same rules.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <ul class="tile-grid">
    <li><a class="tile" href="/components/"><p class="tile__title">Components</p><p class="tile__desc">44 documented components — usage, code, specifications, accessibility.</p></a></li>
    <li><a class="tile" href="/tokens/"><p class="tile__title">Design tokens</p><p class="tile__desc">Every variable with per-theme values, click-to-copy.</p></a></li>
    <li><a class="tile" href="/foundations/"><p class="tile__title">Foundations</p><p class="tile__desc">Typography, theming, spacing, and the token architecture.</p></a></li>
    <li><a class="tile" href="/storybook/" target="_blank"><p class="tile__title">Storybook ↗</p><p class="tile__desc">The interactive workshop behind every example on this site.</p></a></li>
  </ul>
</Page>
